# Tells Git which local, machine-generated, or secret files never belong in
# version control: the virtual environment, Python bytecode caches, tool
# caches, generated experiment outputs, and the real .env file holding API
# keys. It does not affect what gets published once a file is committed.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.env
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
# Exception: the nine real, audited V2 grid-run directories (Milestone 16,
# 2026-08-20) are committed on purpose so a fresh deploy of webapp/ (which
# has no persistent disk on a free host) always ships with real results —
# see README.md's "Using the webapp" section. Every other outputs/ entry
# (calibration/smoke runs, older duplicate runs, anything a sandbox visitor
# generates) stays untracked.
!outputs/baseline_port_closure_comparison__20260820T130134Z/
!outputs/light_port_disruption_comparison__20260820T120030Z/
!outputs/heavy_port_disruption_comparison__20260820T135336Z/
!outputs/compact_light_comparison__20260820T115857Z/
!outputs/compact_medium_comparison__20260820T121936Z/
!outputs/compact_heavy_comparison__20260820T124545Z/
!outputs/extended_light_comparison__20260820T120110Z/
!outputs/extended_medium_comparison__20260820T123415Z/
!outputs/extended_heavy_comparison__20260820T133353Z/
.DS_Store